# Selecting text in the page view, on what the app reports. No event is posted: these go through what a real press, drag and release call.
# recto qa run <a copy of app/qa/selection.qa in a temp folder, where a quiet run reads scripts>, with RECTO_QA_PDF set to a PDF of at least 2 pages whose first line is 12 pt text near the top left of page 1, about 68 points down: `recto select 1` says where.
open "$RECTO_QA_PDF"
qa wait-settled --timeout 30s
qa state
expect reader.selection.selected false
expect app.pages.highlight_layers 0
# A double-click takes a word, once its page is read.
qa mouse-down 1:80,68:2
qa mouse-up
qa wait-settled --timeout 30s
qa state
expect reader.selection.selected true
expect reader.selection.unit word
expect app.pages.highlight_layers 1
# A click clears it.
qa mouse-down 1:80,68
qa mouse-up
qa wait-settled --timeout 30s
qa state
expect reader.selection.selected false
expect app.pages.highlight_layers 0
# Over a page break, zoomed out so both pages show.
qa zoom 0.5
qa wait-settled --timeout 30s
qa mouse-down 1:80,68
qa mouse-drag 2:300,68
qa mouse-up
qa wait-settled --timeout 30s
qa state
expect reader.selection.selected true
expect reader.selection.start.page 1
expect reader.selection.end.page 2
expect app.pages.highlight_layers 2
qa zoom 1
qa wait-settled --timeout 30s
# Select all, and copy, with the menu bar's own items.
qa menu edit.select_all
qa wait-settled --timeout 30s
qa state
expect reader.selection.selected true
qa menu edit.copy
qa wait-settled --timeout 30s
qa copied
expect-at-least chars 1
qa state
expect hangs.over_2s 0
